From 0b04dd6fd15f87430dd34c4dab7861f027c5e9ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Lapshenkov <alexander.lapshenkov@lge.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:39:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [build][webos] 158.0.8127.0~1: V8: Build Torque before
 v8_initializers

v8_initializers compiles sources that include Torque-generated headers, but
the dependencies of the target did not order those compilations after the
run_torque action. A clean build started to fail with the error:

  torque-generated/exported-macros-assembler.h: file not found

To avoid this error :run_torque is added to the deps of v8_initializers.
gn now emits inputdeps with the action, and every compilation of the target
waits for the generated headers.

Test Scenario:

1. Start mksnapshot-cross-aarch64 build:
   . oe-init-build-env
   bitbake -c cleanall mksnapshot-cross-aarch64
   bitbake mksnapshot-cross-aarch64
2. Check that v8 build success.

Issue: NEVA-11578
---
 BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/BUILD.gn b/BUILD.gn
index 0f374d70817..1e50fb72fba 100644
--- a/BUILD.gn
+++ b/BUILD.gn
@@ -3786,2 +3786,3 @@ v8_cluster_source_set("v8_initializers") {
   deps = [
+    ":run_torque",
     ":torque_generated_initializers",
--
2.34.1

